<title>FRANCE: Credit Agricole ups Suez stake.</title>
<headline>Credit Agricole ups Suez stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Co-operative bank Caisse Nationale de Credit Agricole raised its stake in French holding company Cie de Suez on September 12 to 5.04 percent from about 4.9 percent, French stock markets watchdog SBF said.</p>
<p>Credit Agricole's stake represents 9,482,071 voting rights.</p>
<p>With the increase, the bank becomes the third largest shareholder in Suez, after Saint Gobain and Union des Assurances de Paris. Elf Aquitaine is the fourth largest with five percent of the voting rights.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
